**Proposition 9.3 (finite local verification domain).** Exhaustive finite
checks of CSA.2 for $1\le q\le7$ give 3279 optional-register states
and 42648 legal single-slot construction/assignment cases. They satisfy
distinct absent/0/1 support and terminal decoding, terminal prefix closure,
$V_R=2q-1+4c$, $L_R=q+2c$, and the four-vertex/two-leaf construction
increments. The two fresh-bit endpoint templates have reciprocal edges,
four new vertices and exactly 30 initialization/root assignments. All
256 eight-track cell values have 47 vertices, 24 leaves, distinct terminal
sets and exact bit decoding.

Proof. Enumerate the $3^q$ ternary slot words, substitute the three
literal socket trees into the recursive $F_q$, and independently read
the terminal/fork cases at its fixed socket paths. For each state and
slot assign either bit; count vertices and leaves before and after.
Taking all prefixes of all terminal paths returns the full support in
every case. The totals are $\sum_{q=1}^7 3^q=3279$ and
$\sum_{q=1}^7 2q3^q=42648$. For each fresh-bit value initialize four
seven-slot records and the two old root children; every occupied endpoint
has its inverse partner. For the cell check substitute all eight-bit
words into $F_8$. These exact finite enumerations have zero failed
assertions. They check local combinatorics and counts, not a complete
expanded RCA execution, ownership integration or a Lean theorem. The
all-cut result rests on the ordinary row induction and supplier premises,
not extrapolation from these finite samples. ∎

